1
00:00:05,264 --> 00:00:07,634
Do you have all of your belongings with you?

2
00:00:07,634 --> 00:00:10,534
Do you have your lunch,
water bottle, and snacks?

3
00:00:10,744 --> 00:00:12,334
Yes!

4
00:00:12,704 --> 00:00:15,574
Fujimoto, Kobato, you have everything, do you?

5
00:00:15,744 --> 00:00:16,874
Yes.

6
00:00:17,244 --> 00:00:19,374
We're going on a picnic.
You're not taking anything?

7
00:00:21,384 --> 00:00:24,044
I'm sorry! I'll go and get my bag!

8
00:00:29,154 --> 00:00:31,094
Kobato, are you all right?

9
00:00:32,024 --> 00:00:34,084
Y-Yes I'm fine.

10
00:00:39,634 --> 00:00:42,774
Kobato.

11
00:00:42,774 --> 00:00:45,604
Kobato.
Dou sureba iin dakke?

12
00:00:45,604 --> 00:00:50,014
Kobato.
Atarimae no kototte itsumo

13
00:00:50,914 --> 00:00:54,214
Muzukashii na

14
00:00:54,214 --> 00:00:56,984
Ureshii toki waratte

15
00:00:56,984 --> 00:01:01,284
Suki na toki ni utaitai dake

16
00:01:01,854 --> 00:01:04,294
Na no ni

17
00:01:05,594 --> 00:01:09,964
Itsuka negai wa kanau to

18
00:01:10,404 --> 00:01:13,674
Demo "itsuka" tte dore kurai?

19
00:01:13,674 --> 00:01:17,164
Machikirenai yo

20
00:01:17,304 --> 00:01:23,074
123! no aizu de ryoute hirogete

21
00:01:23,074 --> 00:01:28,284
Zenshin ni hikari wo atsumete

22
00:01:28,284 --> 00:01:31,124
Doko ni aru no?

23
00:01:31,124 --> 00:01:34,454
Oshiete, watashi ni dekiru koto

24
00:01:34,454 --> 00:01:37,294
Meippai kizu tsuite

25
00:01:37,294 --> 00:01:40,194
Seiippai hashitte

26
00:01:40,194 --> 00:01:44,164
Nan juu kai koronde naite

27
00:01:44,164 --> 00:01:47,204
Sore de mo mada

28
00:01:47,204 --> 00:01:51,234
Akireru kurai

29
00:01:51,704 --> 00:01:55,874
Ashita wo shinjiteru

30
00:02:05,554 --> 00:02:09,524
...Hide-and-Seek.

31
00:02:09,524 --> 00:02:10,924
...Hide-and-Seek.
Oh, it's you, Kobato.

32
00:02:10,924 --> 00:02:11,184
Oh, it's you, Kobato.

33
00:02:11,324 --> 00:02:13,224
Ioryogi-san, let's go!

34
00:02:14,534 --> 00:02:17,224
We're all going on a picnic now!

35
00:02:17,604 --> 00:02:21,574
Oh I see. I thought you seemed awfully excited.

36
00:02:21,574 --> 00:02:24,104
Yes. Everyone is very excited!

37
00:02:24,104 --> 00:02:26,374
So come with us, Ioryogi-san!

38
00:02:27,144 --> 00:02:28,664
Could be fun.

39
00:02:31,844 --> 00:02:34,084
Oh, u-um...

40
00:02:34,084 --> 00:02:36,754
What are you waiting for?! Pick up the phone!

41
00:02:36,754 --> 00:02:37,914
Y-Yes!

42
00:02:41,454 --> 00:02:43,184
Hello! Kobato Hanato speaking!

43
00:02:44,624 --> 00:02:45,724
Kobato?

44
00:02:45,724 --> 00:02:48,754
Oh! I made a mistake! Yomogi Kindergarten!

45
00:02:48,894 --> 00:02:50,064
Who are you?

46
00:02:50,064 --> 00:02:52,794
I'm just someone helping here.

47
00:02:53,434 --> 00:02:54,974
You're certainly full of energy.

48
00:02:54,974 --> 00:02:56,764
Uh, thank you very much!

49
00:02:58,444 --> 00:03:01,174
Where's Sayaka? I'd like to speak to her.

50
00:03:01,614 --> 00:03:04,944
Uh, well um... we're all on our
way out for a picnic.

51
00:03:04,944 --> 00:03:06,384
Do you have business with her?

52
00:03:06,784 --> 00:03:08,754
That's right. I have business with her.

53
00:03:09,314 --> 00:03:10,984
Will you give her a message?

54
00:03:11,184 --> 00:03:12,414
Sure!

55
00:03:12,824 --> 00:03:15,684
Tell her to shut down the silly
kindergarten and move out.

56
00:03:18,094 --> 00:03:20,154
I'm not extending the repayment deadline.

57
00:03:25,064 --> 00:03:26,964
Are you a debt collector?

58
00:03:28,204 --> 00:03:31,264
You people came to the kindergarten
the other day to bully everybody!

59
00:03:32,744 --> 00:03:34,974
Those guys did such a thing?

60
00:03:36,714 --> 00:03:38,344
Huh? Oh, I-I'm sorry!

61
00:03:38,984 --> 00:03:40,654
Why are you apologizing?

62
00:03:40,654 --> 00:03:45,054
Um, it seems I got mad at you
for something you didn't do.

63
00:03:49,854 --> 00:03:51,794
You're a funny kid!

64
00:03:52,164 --> 00:03:53,284
What's going on?

65
00:03:58,064 --> 00:04:00,964
I hate to tell you this, but your
days of helping are over.

66
00:04:06,974 --> 00:04:08,604
I'm shutting down the kindergarten.

67
00:04:11,684 --> 00:04:13,204
No way...

68
00:04:14,914 --> 00:04:18,044
You be sure and tell that to Sayaka.

69
00:04:18,554 --> 00:04:20,114
U-Um, who are you?

70
00:04:25,224 --> 00:04:27,124
Shutting down the kindergarten...

71
00:04:27,864 --> 00:04:31,164
Do you think Ms. Sayaka knows this person?

72
00:04:36,534 --> 00:04:37,874
I'm passing on the picnic.

73
00:04:38,674 --> 00:04:40,144
Ioryogi-san?

74
00:04:42,344 --> 00:04:44,214
I'm going home for a nap.

75
00:04:52,684 --> 00:04:53,654
You took forever!

76
00:04:53,654 --> 00:04:57,054
Man... How long must you keep us waiting?

77
00:04:57,694 --> 00:05:00,064
Thanks to you, we're off to a late start.

78
00:05:01,664 --> 00:05:05,994
U-Um. Is the debt collector an
acquaintance of Ms. Sayaka's?

79
00:05:06,864 --> 00:05:07,834
What?

80
00:05:08,304 --> 00:05:11,704
There was a call a moment ago. From a man.

81
00:05:12,274 --> 00:05:13,904
Said he's shutting down the kindergarten.

82
00:05:15,674 --> 00:05:16,944
It's him.

83
00:05:18,144 --> 00:05:20,474
Don't tell Ms. Sayaka about the call.

84
00:05:21,114 --> 00:05:24,714
But, but, he sounded pretty scary.

85
00:05:28,424 --> 00:05:29,944
Anyway, just keep quiet about it.

86
00:05:37,234 --> 00:05:40,464
Kobato! Fujimoto! We're leaving!

87
00:05:41,074 --> 00:05:43,034
Sorry. We'll be right there.

88
00:05:57,984 --> 00:06:01,884
The entrances are always
in the strangest places.

89
00:06:15,134 --> 00:06:18,534
Bear's Baumkuchen Shop

90
00:06:31,684 --> 00:06:32,884
Hello there!

91
00:06:35,424 --> 00:06:36,554
Hi.

92
00:06:36,554 --> 00:06:38,284
Oh it's you.

93
00:06:38,594 --> 00:06:41,654
I expected more originality in
the name of your shop!

94
00:06:42,134 --> 00:06:43,534
Well, what did you expect?

95
00:06:44,104 --> 00:06:47,864
He told me what to name the shop when
he handed me my occupation.

96
00:06:48,434 --> 00:06:50,964
The guy decides everything, does he?!

97
00:06:52,044 --> 00:06:53,474
Don't call him "the guy."

98
00:06:55,114 --> 00:06:57,844
You get turned into a toy, and still
you haven't learnt your lesson!

99
00:06:57,844 --> 00:06:59,114
I have no lesson to learn!

100
00:06:59,114 --> 00:07:00,674
I haven't done anything wrong!

101
00:07:00,854 --> 00:07:04,474
I can't believe you're still talking like that after
all the ruckus you caused! You idiot!

102
00:07:06,824 --> 00:07:10,814
They hear you talking like that and you're
not getting away with being a toy doll!

103
00:07:11,424 --> 00:07:12,914
They'll reduce you to the size of a thumb doll!

104
00:07:15,734 --> 00:07:17,724
Well, we'll leave that aside for now.

105
00:07:17,934 --> 00:07:19,634
What the heck brings you here today?

106
00:07:19,634 --> 00:07:21,434
Hm? Right...

107
00:07:22,604 --> 00:07:24,574
What is it? Spit it out.

108
00:07:25,374 --> 00:07:27,904
I need you to look into something for me.

109
00:07:31,414 --> 00:07:34,674
Anyway, have a seat. I can at least
hear what you have to say.

110
00:07:37,684 --> 00:07:40,914
Woah!

111
00:07:41,324 --> 00:07:42,724
Look how high we are!

112
00:07:46,794 --> 00:07:47,954
Hey! Look over there!

113
00:07:48,034 --> 00:07:48,964
What is it?

114
00:07:49,064 --> 00:07:50,364
It's a large lake!

115
00:07:50,804 --> 00:07:52,564
I'm shutting down the kindergarten.

116
00:07:53,904 --> 00:07:57,234
I wonder who that was on
the phone this morning.

117
00:07:59,144 --> 00:08:00,264
Kobato!

118
00:08:00,414 --> 00:08:01,674
Toshihiko!

119
00:08:01,874 --> 00:08:05,784
Marina! It's time for lunch!

120
00:08:05,844 --> 00:08:07,334
Okay!

121
00:08:13,684 --> 00:08:16,024
I have a bump here now.

122
00:08:16,154 --> 00:08:19,094
Kobato, you've been through a lot of pain today.

123
00:08:19,624 --> 00:08:21,624
Your attention seems to be elsewhere.

124
00:08:21,894 --> 00:08:24,334
Is there something bothering you, Kobato?

125
00:08:25,104 --> 00:08:26,504
Oh, well...

126
00:08:27,004 --> 00:08:29,734
She's always an airhead.

127
00:08:30,474 --> 00:08:32,164
Not always!

128
00:08:33,144 --> 00:08:36,604
Don't you get Ms. Sayaka worrying
more than she needs to.

129
00:08:38,884 --> 00:08:40,174
Right.

130
00:08:45,884 --> 00:08:48,494
So you're looking for information regarding
the state of Yomogi Kindergarten

131
00:08:48,494 --> 00:08:50,754
and persons associated with it?

132
00:08:51,524 --> 00:08:52,784
Yeah.

133
00:08:53,964 --> 00:08:57,604
What wrong? Did that pathetic new look
strip you of the investigation skills

134
00:08:57,604 --> 00:08:59,434
you used to brag about?

135
00:08:59,834 --> 00:09:03,894
Your looks are tens of thousands of times
more pathetic looking than mine.

136
00:09:04,574 --> 00:09:07,974
I never expected you to talk
to me in that way though.

137
00:09:08,074 --> 00:09:09,044
Huh?

138
00:09:09,044 --> 00:09:11,874
Back then you'd just say "check it".

139
00:09:12,184 --> 00:09:15,674
And if I didn't do as you said, you'd
breathe fire or throw your fist at me.

140
00:09:16,754 --> 00:09:20,994
In that case, I'll give you your wish!
Extra special!

141
00:09:20,994 --> 00:09:23,114
Cut that out already!

142
00:09:24,064 --> 00:09:25,454
Oh, it's done.

143
00:09:25,724 --> 00:09:28,134
This job's too perfect for you!

144
00:09:28,134 --> 00:09:29,624
You're fitting right in I see!

145
00:09:34,634 --> 00:09:38,304
If your men back then saw you
now, they'd be in tears.

146
00:09:39,244 --> 00:09:42,074
The last thing I need is a stuffed
toy telling me that.

147
00:09:42,574 --> 00:09:43,874
Watch your words!

148
00:09:44,414 --> 00:09:46,814
I'll look into it for you.

149
00:09:48,114 --> 00:09:49,884
It's got something to do with that girl, right?

150
00:09:51,484 --> 00:09:52,574
Thanks, man.

151
00:09:53,954 --> 00:09:57,414
Well, especially since you "asked" this time.

152
00:09:57,524 --> 00:09:58,024
This is pretty good.

153
00:09:58,024 --> 00:09:58,764
Woah! Who said you could have any?!
This is pretty good.

154
00:09:58,764 --> 00:10:00,784
Woah! Who said you could have any?!

155
00:10:09,174 --> 00:10:10,434
Kobato.

156
00:10:12,944 --> 00:10:14,274
Marina.

157
00:10:15,714 --> 00:10:17,004
What can I do for you?

158
00:10:17,744 --> 00:10:20,714
Kobato, is there something worrying you?

159
00:10:21,414 --> 00:10:25,584
Uh, no... well... um... No there isn't!
Nothing! I'm positive!

160
00:10:26,954 --> 00:10:28,114
So there is something.

161
00:10:31,064 --> 00:10:33,854
It's okay. I'll tell you something good.

162
00:10:35,294 --> 00:10:38,134
If you find it you can be happy.

163
00:10:40,874 --> 00:10:42,924
Kobato! Marina!

164
00:10:43,374 --> 00:10:45,164
Let's play hide-and-seek!

165
00:10:46,674 --> 00:10:48,164
All right!

166
00:10:48,914 --> 00:10:50,974
I'll be right there!

167
00:10:52,744 --> 00:10:59,584
Rock, paper, scissors! One,
two, three! One, two...

168
00:10:59,584 --> 00:11:00,784
Three!

169
00:11:01,924 --> 00:11:03,944
Kobato, you're it!

170
00:11:06,594 --> 00:11:12,124
While you're counting to ten, Kobato, we're all
going to hide. Then come and find us.

171
00:11:17,374 --> 00:11:20,434
Okay! Kobato is ready!

172
00:11:48,734 --> 00:11:51,744
Is this all I get? Darn.

173
00:11:51,744 --> 00:11:54,474
I'm telling you, I could pile dozens of these!

174
00:11:54,714 --> 00:11:57,574
Damn it! This body of mine can be such a pain!

175
00:11:58,344 --> 00:12:00,214
Pretty pathetic too.

176
00:12:03,914 --> 00:12:05,974
I really didn't need to hear that from you.

177
00:12:11,824 --> 00:12:14,054
It's been awhile, Ginsei.

178
00:12:17,704 --> 00:12:20,194
You really do look pathetic.

179
00:12:20,634 --> 00:12:21,934
You shut your face!

180
00:12:49,664 --> 00:12:53,464
So I see you've changed on the outside but
you're still the same on the inside.

181
00:12:56,634 --> 00:12:58,734
Aren't you ever returning to "Ikai"?

182
00:13:00,044 --> 00:13:01,564
I've got things to do.

183
00:13:02,814 --> 00:13:04,434
It's that little girl.

184
00:13:05,914 --> 00:13:08,744
You set one finger on Kobato and
I'll have you for lunch.

185
00:13:14,194 --> 00:13:18,324
Don't you forget, we still haven't
had our deciding match.

186
00:13:28,274 --> 00:13:30,364
What a pain...

187
00:13:34,914 --> 00:13:37,974
Where could everyone have hidden?

188
00:13:50,154 --> 00:13:51,884
They're not anywhere.

189
00:14:00,104 --> 00:14:03,004
Where are you, everybody?!

190
00:14:03,534 --> 00:14:06,304
Oh? Kobato sure seems to be having fun.

191
00:14:07,674 --> 00:14:10,834
Kobato still hasn't even found one of us yet.

192
00:14:11,544 --> 00:14:14,144
Oh, she's looking in some strange place again.

193
00:14:15,814 --> 00:14:17,304
Looks like they'll be awhile.

194
00:14:18,224 --> 00:14:21,294
Everyone, you are very good at hiding.

195
00:14:21,294 --> 00:14:22,624
Hey!

196
00:14:23,524 --> 00:14:24,894
Fujimoto.

197
00:14:24,894 --> 00:14:26,464
We should get going!

198
00:14:26,464 --> 00:14:29,224
Not yet! I'm it right now!

199
00:14:29,594 --> 00:14:30,734
Huh?

200
00:14:30,734 --> 00:14:33,754
The person who's it must find
the ones that are hiding!

201
00:14:34,604 --> 00:14:36,834
Yeah, but it's time to go.

202
00:14:38,344 --> 00:14:40,574
Come on out! We're going home!

203
00:14:42,014 --> 00:14:43,474
Okay!

204
00:14:43,744 --> 00:14:44,644
Oh!

205
00:14:44,644 --> 00:14:46,514
There they are!

206
00:14:50,184 --> 00:14:52,314
K-Kobato are you okay?

207
00:14:53,754 --> 00:14:56,624
Toshihiko and Yoshio! I found you!

208
00:14:57,054 --> 00:14:58,284
Huh?

209
00:14:59,824 --> 00:15:01,124
She's right!

210
00:15:01,194 --> 00:15:02,684
She found us!

211
00:15:05,634 --> 00:15:07,964
Yuzuru and Yukari! I found you!

212
00:15:08,234 --> 00:15:10,294
Oh, Masao! I found you!

213
00:15:10,704 --> 00:15:12,104
And there are more of you over there!

214
00:15:13,874 --> 00:15:15,504
Oh, there too!

215
00:15:16,844 --> 00:15:18,334
Over there too!

216
00:15:21,454 --> 00:15:24,044
Kobato, you've still got a leaf on your head!

217
00:15:24,354 --> 00:15:26,584
You're so silly. Let me get it for you.

218
00:15:26,984 --> 00:15:28,884
Thank you very much.

219
00:15:28,994 --> 00:15:30,514
Shall we go then?

220
00:15:31,264 --> 00:15:32,554
Okay!

221
00:15:32,994 --> 00:15:36,194
Let's take a group picture before we go.

222
00:15:38,404 --> 00:15:39,334
Oh?

223
00:15:39,604 --> 00:15:41,064
Where's Marina?

224
00:15:44,844 --> 00:15:46,274
I don't see her.

225
00:15:49,344 --> 00:15:50,814
Let me go look for her.

226
00:15:51,114 --> 00:15:52,374
Fujimoto.

227
00:15:52,814 --> 00:15:55,344
Ms. Sayaka, please stay
here with the others.

228
00:15:56,214 --> 00:15:57,984
I-I'll go and look for her, too.

229
00:16:02,124 --> 00:16:02,924
Marina!

230
00:16:02,924 --> 00:16:03,914
Marina!
Marina!

231
00:16:04,364 --> 00:16:07,254
Marina!

232
00:16:09,134 --> 00:16:11,034
Marina!

233
00:16:11,934 --> 00:16:13,404
Marina!

234
00:16:14,604 --> 00:16:16,294
Marina!

235
00:16:18,074 --> 00:16:18,944
Did you find her?

236
00:16:18,944 --> 00:16:22,634
No. I wonder if she's still hiding somewhere.

237
00:16:23,014 --> 00:16:24,444
Let's wish.

238
00:16:26,044 --> 00:16:28,884
If I could only have found her sooner.

239
00:16:35,224 --> 00:16:36,524
Let's search over there.

240
00:16:39,824 --> 00:16:42,734
Marina!

241
00:16:44,234 --> 00:16:45,704
Marina!

242
00:17:08,594 --> 00:17:09,924
Marina?!

243
00:17:19,604 --> 00:17:21,154
She's asleep.

244
00:17:23,504 --> 00:17:25,374
What a relief.

245
00:17:27,744 --> 00:17:29,004
Marina.

246
00:17:32,684 --> 00:17:34,204
Hello there.

247
00:17:35,884 --> 00:17:37,544
Kobato...

248
00:17:39,084 --> 00:17:41,574
Sorry I couldn't find any.

249
00:17:42,224 --> 00:17:43,784
You mean with hide-and-seek?

250
00:17:44,464 --> 00:17:47,394
No, a four-leaf clover.

251
00:17:49,664 --> 00:17:56,004
If you find it, you can be happy.
I wanted to find one for you.

252
00:17:57,074 --> 00:17:58,264
For me?!

253
00:17:58,604 --> 00:18:04,014
Mhm. You didn't seem too happy today, so...

254
00:18:09,684 --> 00:18:12,674
I looked everywhere, but I couldn't find one.

255
00:18:13,454 --> 00:18:14,644
I'm sorry.

256
00:18:21,134 --> 00:18:23,894
It's okay even if you didn't find one.

257
00:18:27,434 --> 00:18:34,464
I'm fine. Because you went and searched for
my happiness. So now I'm happy!

258
00:18:38,444 --> 00:18:40,104
I'm glad!

259
00:18:45,754 --> 00:18:48,584
There's a nice view. Let's take a picture here.

260
00:18:54,224 --> 00:18:56,224
Okay now, don't anybody move!

261
00:18:56,564 --> 00:18:58,494
Fujimoto! Hurry!

262
00:18:58,804 --> 00:19:00,894
I'm okay. You just face the front.

263
00:19:11,884 --> 00:19:13,314
What now?

264
00:19:15,054 --> 00:19:16,674
I found one.

265
00:19:21,354 --> 00:19:23,294
A four-leaf clover.

266
00:19:28,664 --> 00:19:29,924
Here you are.

267
00:19:30,764 --> 00:19:32,824
Thank you, Kobato!

268
00:19:36,474 --> 00:19:38,494
Kobato, look, look!

269
00:19:39,244 --> 00:19:40,434
Look here!

270
00:19:41,114 --> 00:19:43,134
They're all over!

271
00:19:45,314 --> 00:19:48,684
We found lots and lots of happiness.

272
00:19:49,214 --> 00:19:50,284
Hey!

273
00:19:50,284 --> 00:19:51,984
We're taking another picture!

274
00:19:51,984 --> 00:19:53,784
Okay!

275
00:20:07,534 --> 00:20:08,404
Oh no!

276
00:20:08,404 --> 00:20:12,964
Your cake is all crumbled. Cake that
Sir Genko specially gave you.

277
00:20:14,574 --> 00:20:17,404
What is it with you all, one after another?

278
00:20:21,954 --> 00:20:24,544
You're the little helper at the big bear's place.

279
00:20:25,124 --> 00:20:27,454
Uh... I know your name... uh...

280
00:20:28,554 --> 00:20:29,294
Nope. I forgot.

281
00:20:29,294 --> 00:20:30,554
Oh, come on!

282
00:20:32,194 --> 00:20:33,754
The name is Zuisho!

283
00:20:33,894 --> 00:20:35,654
I have a message for you from Sir Genko!

284
00:20:35,794 --> 00:20:38,024
Your requested investigation is complete!

285
00:20:38,204 --> 00:20:39,304
What?!

286
00:20:39,304 --> 00:20:41,064
Hey! Good on him!

287
00:20:41,204 --> 00:20:43,674
Your form doesn't quite suit your cool smile.

288
00:20:44,604 --> 00:20:46,504
Don't be cheeky with me, birdie!

289
00:20:53,244 --> 00:20:56,014
I'm home! Huh?

290
00:20:59,054 --> 00:21:02,184
Ioryogi-san is not home yet.

291
00:21:06,364 --> 00:21:10,494
Oh no! He's so small, perhaps he
got stuck somewhere!

292
00:21:10,494 --> 00:21:12,904
Or maybe he fell off the side of a road!

293
00:21:12,904 --> 00:21:15,524
Or maybe someone squished him!

294
00:21:15,634 --> 00:21:17,404
Oh no, this is a problem!

295
00:21:17,404 --> 00:21:19,464
Ioryogi-san is in big trouble!

296
00:21:20,444 --> 00:21:22,074
Who's in big trouble?

297
00:21:22,074 --> 00:21:23,544
Ioryogi-san!

298
00:21:24,614 --> 00:21:25,644
Hey.

299
00:21:25,644 --> 00:21:27,114
Welcome home.

300
00:21:29,254 --> 00:21:30,914
What's that?

301
00:21:32,284 --> 00:21:33,914
Oh, this?

302
00:21:34,524 --> 00:21:35,924
It's a Baumkuchen.

303
00:21:37,524 --> 00:21:39,394
So how was the picnic?

304
00:21:40,194 --> 00:21:42,924
I have something for you, Ioryogi-san!

305
00:21:43,764 --> 00:21:44,854
Here!

306
00:21:45,204 --> 00:21:46,994
It's a four leaf clover of happiness.

307
00:21:47,064 --> 00:21:52,024
It's a little shriveled, but I found
some happiness for you, too!

308
00:21:55,644 --> 00:21:59,134
I want everybody to stay happy, forever.

309
00:21:59,884 --> 00:22:02,284
Especially everyone at Yomogi Kindergarten.

310
00:22:08,554 --> 00:22:11,364
I report! Regarding Yomogi Kindergarten!

311
00:22:11,364 --> 00:22:14,654
The former principal was apparently
tricked into borrowing money!

312
00:22:15,194 --> 00:22:16,634
Former principal?

313
00:22:16,934 --> 00:22:22,424
Yes. Sayaka Okiura's father.
He died two years ago.

314
00:22:26,344 --> 00:22:29,004
Looks like a real bad bunch who tricked him.

315
00:22:29,274 --> 00:22:33,684
Not only that, one of them seems to
be a relative of Sayaka Okiura.

316
00:22:34,814 --> 00:22:37,184
Sounds like a bit of a mess.

317
00:22:38,884 --> 00:22:45,344
So basically, if left alone, sooner or later Yomogi
Kindergarten will be forced to shut down.

318
00:23:01,314 --> 00:23:08,944
Hito wa mina tonde mitai no ni

319
00:23:10,114 --> 00:23:16,214
Juuryoku ni damasareterunda

320
00:23:16,494 --> 00:23:24,334
Dare mo honto wa toberunda yo

321
00:23:26,564 --> 00:23:32,904
Ano ko ga anna ni kanashisou na no wa

322
00:23:33,944 --> 00:23:36,814
Jibun no kage wo

323
00:23:36,814 --> 00:23:43,944
Dokoka ni wasurete kichatta kara kamo

324
00:23:44,114 --> 00:23:46,644
Sore nara

325
00:23:46,824 --> 00:23:50,924
"Arigatou," tte kimi ni ietara

326
00:23:50,924 --> 00:23:54,794
"Arigatou," tte kimi ga waraeba

327
00:23:54,794 --> 00:24:02,134
Ittari kitari ureshiku naru

328
00:24:02,674 --> 00:24:06,904
Kimi ga shiawase ni naru

329
00:24:07,204 --> 00:24:11,444
Shinpai nante iranai yo

330
00:24:11,444 --> 00:24:15,544
Issho ni iru kara

331
00:24:17,314 --> 00:24:23,254
Ureshikuttemo namida ga deru nante

332
00:24:23,254 --> 00:24:26,124
Fushigi da

333
00:24:26,124 --> 00:24:28,994
Next episode
...Gentle Person.
Fushigi da

334
00:24:28,994 --> 00:24:30,794
Next episode
...Gentle Person.

